  "published": "2026-07-27T06:18:05.237Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes CC001 code fix for async iterators: it now adds [EnumeratorCancellation] and the System.Runtime.CompilerServices import alongside the CancellationToken parameter. On an iterator a bare token is ignored by the compiler-generated GetAsyncEnumerator, so a consumer .WithCancellation(token) silently fails to reach it — which is what CC011 reports — meaning the fix previously traded CC001 for CC011 and left the stream just as uncancellable. Ordinary async methods still get a plain token, since the attribute on a non-iterator is a compiler error. Diagnostic IDs and severities are unchanged from 1.34.0.",
